================================================================================
Figures for "Gyre dynamics modulate northward throughput of Gulf Stream water to subpolar latitudes" 
===============================================================================
Code accompanying the Lagrangian particle trajectory dataset [DOI TO DATSET]

Repository: https://github.com/heleneasb/traj_code

OVERVIEW
--------
Code producing the figures in the manuscript "Gyre dynamics modulate northward throughput of Gulf Stream water to subpolar latitudes". 

REQUIREMENTS
-------------
Language : Python 3.9.13

Python packages:
    numpy==1.26.4
    xarray==2024.3.0
    pandas==2.2.3 
    cartopy==0.20.3 
    matplotlib==3.5.1
    gsw==3.6.20 
    scipy==1.10.1 
    dask==2024.8.0 

External datasets required (not included in this repository):
    - Lagrangian trajectory data from experiment 'gulfstream_GO8p7'
      Source/access: [DOI TO DATASET]
    - GO8p7-eORCA12-JRA55 ocean hindcast output
      Variables: meridional velocity, zonal velocity, conservative temperature, absolute salinity
      Source/access: [https://dx.doi.org/10.5285/399b0f762a004657a411a9ea7203493a]
    - JRA-55 atmospheric reanalysis
      Variable: Sea level pressure
      Source/access: [https://doi.org/10.5065/D60G3H5B]

HOW TO RUN
------------
IMPORTANT: The .py scripts must be run BEFORE the .ipynb notebooks. The .py
scripts perform the required data preparation/processing steps that the
notebooks depend on.

Step 1 -- Download required datasets

Step 2 -- Run the Python scripts, in order

Step 3 -- Run the notebooks

